   assert len(items) >= 2, \"expected at least two nested foreground rectangles\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6cbe9eb8.py:54:    assert len(areas) == len(set(areas)), \"rectangle areas must define a unique nesting order\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6cbe9eb8.py:80:    Rebuild the foreground rectangles as a largest-to-smallest lower-left nesting.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6cbe9eb8.py:83:    - A periodic wallpaper background is overlaid by foreground colors that each form a rectangular frame or solid rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6cbe9eb8.py:84:    - The largest foreground rectangle is the output frame; smaller foreground rectangles are the objects to nest inside it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6cbe9eb8.py:85:    - A frame may be partially hidden by a smaller rectangle, but its visible pixels still determine its bbox.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6cbe9eb8.py:88:    - Ignore the wallpaper and crop the result to the largest foreground rectangle's bbox size.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6cbe9eb8.py:89:    - Sort foreground rectangles by bbox area from largest to smallest.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6cbe9eb8.py:90:    - Reconstruct each frame or solid rectangle, placing every next smaller rectangle in the lower-left of the current rectangle's usable region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6cbe9eb8.py:93:    - The scattered background colors are not objects; the meaningful order is the unique descending rectangle size chain, and each step nests into the previous rectangle's lower-left interior.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6cbe9eb8.py:98:    items = _foreground_rectangles(g)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6cbe9eb8.py:107:        assert h <= rh and w <= rw, \"nested rectangle must fit in parent usable region\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6cbe9eb8.py:124:# Solid rectangle dimensions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6cbe9eb8.py:132:# Wal